    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hipatterns\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be great if there was a builtin support for hex shortcuts and alpha component. You can see an example below where I list 4 different ways of defining a red color. \r\n\r\n```css\r\nbody {\r\n  color: #ff0000; /* the only one that currently supported */\r\n  color: #f00;\r\n  color: #ff000000;\r\n  color: #f000;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n[MDN documentation about HEX](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/hex-color)\r\n\r\nOther plugins that support hex shortcut and alpha channels:\r\n- [ccc.nvim](https://github.com/uga-rosa/ccc.nvim)\r\n- [nvim-colorizer.lua](https://github.com/NvChad/nvim-colorizer.lua)\r\n\r\nPS: thank you for your work!",
    "closed_at": "2023-06-17T15:22:00Z",
